Deterministic chain-rule proof of E18 that does not use the manuscript's root-swap invariance step. Shown in the review:
- the factorization 12[v-(v-bu)t]^2 + b^3 t^2 - 3b^2 = 3(t-1)(Lt-N);
- the degree-drop identity 12k D_cub^2 + B^3 = 3k^3 L/Z^6;
- the separate b=0 case;
- det DPhi = 6k^3 g/Z^8 in (u,v,Z) order;
- the exact identities g(T) = -t_c^3 g, N(T) = N t_c^4, L(T) = L t_c^6, hence det DT = -t_c^4 and Q(T) = -t_c^7 Q.
