Full new conventional derivation 'Actual global elder labels, Borel first-death selections and weighted exhaustion' (ELDER_EXHAUSTION_ACTUAL_SOURCE_BRIDGE_ATTACK_20261008.md, 29816 B, SHA256 f378c9d8...4c9a), in 10 sections, with the full exact review. It proves:
- the coefficient-to-field map yields a Borel C2 field;
- the Morse/distinct-value locus admits complete locally continuous critical branches (parametric implicit function theorem) on a countable Borel partition;
- the strict path test T with a positive rational clearance is jointly Borel; the function (a - sqrt(2)/2)^2 is a counterexample showing a test without the margin fails;
- the closed-level relation R = for all m, T(s-1/m) is exactly same-component in X_s, via nested compact connected components and local path connectedness;
- Borel first-death saddle and immediate (not final-root) elder parent P_M;
- the Borel atoms are exactly the barcode bars, counted with multiplicity;
- weighted Kac-Rice extends to the elder mark by monotone class;
- all nonprincipal populations are O_(n,L)(1) = o(ell^(-1/3)), which composes the fixed-(n,L) leading theorem nu_all(ell) = c_(n,L) ell^(-1/3) + R(ell).

Full final Lean source of MorseCongruence.lean (5440 B, SHA256 a922aa09...262e), with tests and audit. On Sym n = selfAdjoint.submodule R (Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) R) it defines polynomial A(S) = J + 2S + project(SJS) and proves:
- polynomial_contDiff;
- polynomial_hasFDerivAt_zero (derivative 2 Id, via doubleEquiv with inverse (1/2) Id);
- polynomial_congruence: A(S) = (1+JS)^* J (1+JS) when J^2 = 1;
- exists_congruence_branch: there is an open V containing J and a map s with s J = 0, ContDiffOn R 2 s V, and M = (1+J s(M))^* J (1+J s(M)) for every M in V, constructed with the implicit function theorem.
Tests cover mixed-sign J, n=0, and the nonzero skew kernel of the full-matrix derivative. The 20-row audit shows only the three standard axioms. main09, tests03 and audit01 exited 0.

